      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ اَلرَّجُلُ يَأْتِي أَخَاهُ وَ هُوَ فِي اَلطَّوَافِ فَقَالَ «يَخْرُجُ مَعَهُ فِي حَاجَتِهِ ثُمَّ يَرْجِعُ وَ يَبْنِي عَلَى طَوَافِهِ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2799 - It is narrated from Safwan al-Jammal, who said: I said to Abu Abdullah (as), \"What about a man who meets his brother while performing tawaf?\"\nImam (as) said: \"He may leave with him to fulfill his need, then return and continue his tawaf from where he left off.\""
        ]
      }
